\item Columns are sorted by name, as UTF-8 bytes (C collation).
\item Every cell is a JSON string, or \code{null} for \code{NA}.
\item Character values are their UTF-8 text, not Unicode-normalized; factors are
their labels.
\item Integers are their decimal digits; logicals are \code{true} and \code{false}.
\item A double with a declared tolerance \code{10^-k} is written with exactly \code{k}
decimals, rounding its exact binary value with ties to even, as C's \code{printf}
and Python's \code{format(x, ".kf")} do. With no tolerance it is written in
ECMAScript's shortest round-trip form, so it is exact. A zero is written
without a sign. \code{NaN} and infinite values abort.
\item Dates are \code{YYYY-MM-DD}. Datetimes are converted to UTC and written
